> ## C73 to C79 against the nPM1304 datasheet (2026-11-13, deferred item 129)
> 
> The bom.csv rows of C73 to C79 say "value from the nPM1300 kit design (DK PCA10184); to confirm against the nPM1304 product specification (S18)". This section is that confirmation. bom.csv is not changed. Sources: design/datasheets/npm1304_datasheet_v1_0.txt (line numbers from grep -n; page = the last "--- page N" marker before the line), design/ecad/ring/pmic-caps-facts.md (G1 to G5), design/wiring/lead-decisions.md row "power chip capacitors against Nordic's datasheet" (line 79), design/ecad/ring/parts.csv and netlist.csv (nets read today).
> 
> - C73, 1.0 uF, GRM033R60J105MEA2D, 0201, net VBUSOUT (chip pin VBUSOUT): value CONFIRMED. The datasheet says "VBUSOUT must have a decoupling capacitor." (line 810, page 16) and its parts lists give "C5", "1.0 μF", "Capacitor, X5R, 10 V, ±10%" (lines 14048 to 14050, page 157; also pages 159 and 160). NOT confirmed: the voltage rating. The datasheet lists 10 V; the ring part's code 0J means 6.3 V by Murata's code (not read in a document: design/datasheets/motor_murata_GRM033R60J105MEA2.pdf is an HTML "Not Found" page, pmic-caps-facts.md G2). Missing: Murata's sheet of this part, to read the rating and the DC bias at the VBUSOUT voltage (the datasheet gives only nominal values for this pin).
> - C74 and C75, 10 uF each, GRM155R60J106ME15D, 0402, net VSYS: value CONFIRMED. The datasheet lists "C2, C3, C4, C7, C8," "10 μF", "Capacitor, X5R, 16 V, ±20%" (lines 14052 to 14055, page 157) and says VSYS "is supplied by its decoupling capacitors" when VBUS is off (line 1636, page 27). The rating (6.3 V, Murata sheet w1d line 52) is under the listed 16 V but above the highest VSYS voltage, because the chip cuts VBUS off above 5.5 V (lines 825 to 828, lead-decisions.md line 79). Not confirmed by the datasheet: the datasheet states no minimum capacitance on VSYS; the bench measures the ripple on VSYS.
> - C76 and C77, 1.0 nF each, no part number, 0201, net VSYS: NOT confirmed. The datasheet has no 1 nF capacitor anywhere (grep for "nF" in the datasheet text finds no capacitor value); its parts list for VSYS has only 10 μF parts. The value comes from the kit design (DK C42) only. Missing: a Nordic statement (kit schematic or datasheet) that asks for it, and a part number (bom.csv evidence tag CALC).
> - C78, 10 uF, GRM155R60J106ME15D, 0402, net VDD_1V8 (buck 1 output, VOUT1): value CONFIRMED. Table 18 asks "Effective capacitance" "≥ 4" "μF" and "ESR" "≤ 50" "mΩ" (lines 3172 to 3177, page 45); the parts list gives 10 μF X5R 16 V (lines 14052 to 14055, page 157). At 1.8 V the Murata graph gives about 6.5 uF (pmic-caps-facts.md G5), above 4 uF, and C4 is also on the net. Not checked: the ESR of this part (no ESR figure read from the Murata sheet).
> - C79, 10 uF, GRM155R60J106ME15D, 0402, net VDD_3V0 (buck 2 output, VOUT2): value NOT confirmed alone. Table 18 asks 4 uF or more effective (page 45, lines 3172 to 3174); the Murata graph gives about 4 uF at 3.0 V for a ±20 percent part: no margin (lead-decisions.md line 79). It is confirmed only together with C90 (second 10 uF on VDD_3V0, parts.csv and netlist.csv today), about 8 uF effective by the same graph. ESR not checked, as for C78.
> 
> Count of the 7: confirmed 4 (C73, C74, C75, C78); confirmed only together with C90 1 (C79); not confirmed 2 (C76, C77). Parts still open inside the confirmed ones: C73 rating, C74 and C75 ripple on the bench, C78 and C79 ESR.
